WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.360
A set of old scales.

2
00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:06.930
Onto one pan drop handcuffs,
a plain wooden peg leg,

3
00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.630
and an iron box.

4
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.890
Onto the other: a broken
promise, a stack of coins,

5
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.920
a sealed attic door.

6
00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:17.990
The scales tip, and never settle.

7
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:22.090
Back at Baker Street, a captured
convict faces the detective.

8
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:23.000
"Justice!"

9
00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.600
snarled the ex-convict.

10
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.470
"A pretty justice!"

11
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.790
He calls his crime justice.

12
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:29.830
Is he right?

13
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.880
And does the novel agree with him?

14
00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:35.350
In this mission, you'll put the
official police beside Holmes,

15
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.630
and see whose judgements hold up.

16
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.020
You'll hear Small's own case
for why the treasure is his.

17
00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:43.770
And you'll ask who in
this novel faces the law,

18
00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:45.470
and who never does.

19
00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.250
Your mission: decide whether
the novel agrees with Small.
